# UI & Component Governance

Follow Decision → Design → Development → Delivery for every UI change.

## Decision
- Search `src/ui` and `src/components` before creating anything. Reuse or extend; do not duplicate.
- Core primitives live in `src/ui` (Button, Field, Card, Spinner). No business/API logic there.
- Screens in `src/pages` and chrome in `src/components` compose primitives.

## Design
- Tokens only: `src/index.css` `@theme` (`canvas`, `ink`, `primary`, `accent`, `line`, `success`, `warning`).
- No new hex, fonts, radii, or one-off padding. No local CSS hacks that mutate globals.
- Interactive pieces must cover default, hover, active, disabled, and `:focus-visible`.

## Development
- Typed props interfaces on every component. Semantic HTML + keyboard access + ARIA.
- Forms: import from `src/ui` (`TextField`, `SelectField`, `TextAreaField`, `SearchSelectField`, `FileField`, `ChoiceField`, `FormGrid`). Controls live in `src/ui/forms`. Do not duplicate local `Field` wrappers or raw `.form-input` markup.

## Delivery
- Do not ship if layout regresses, it is not usable on mobile/tablet/desktop, or focus rings are missing.

```tsx
// BAD — new control + hardcoded color
<button style={{ background: '#2955a3', padding: 11 }}>Save</button>

// GOOD
<Button variant="solid">Save</Button>
```
